Approach:
the file disko-1.dd.gz on opening it using say cat cmd the the webshell gets exahaused and reconnects. 
In such a case we should take the contents of the file and make a zip file by using gunzip disko-1.dd.gz
now as the hint suggests to use the strings function along with the grep cmd to get the output as the flag 
the cmd we use here is strings disko-1.dd | grep picoCTF we get the ctf flag.

